


The hstr_import function "hstr_import.h"

            The hstr_import function clears the character
            array specified by #0, the "array," then copies
            the initial portion of the string pointed to by
            #1, the "string" into the initial portion of the
            array. If #1 is null, the hstr_import function
            behaves as if the string were a null string.

    Returns

            The hstr_import function returns zero if the
            entire string was copied into the array.
            Otherwise, the hstr_function returns a negative
            value, indicating an incomplete copy (the string
            does not fit into the array).
